~ start
Aelric: Is… is this it? The ancient tree… It’s… gone.

Zephros: …Gone? It can’t be. I felt its power just days ago.

Lyra: …This doesn’t look like just death. Something… unnatural happened here.

Aelric: I need to understand… The stories said it holds powers beyond imagination. I… I want to learn from it.

zephros: …Learn? You mean take its power. You’ve always been obsessed.

lyra: Obsessed? You’d risk everything for it… even us. Maybe it’s better if you… stop here.

Aelric: What… What do you mean?

Zephros: We can’t let you do this. You’re too naive. The power of this tree… it’s not meant for someone like you.

lyra: Yeah. It should belong to someone who can control it… someone stronger. Sorry, but… it has to be now.

Aelric: Why… why betray me?

Zephros: Power… survival… sometimes, loyalty dies before ambition.


=> END